    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d678-a2">

                <pb facs="0758" n="678" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg678"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Jérémie to Mr. Powell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State for Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1902-06-04"><hi rendition="#italic">June 4,
                                1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your dispatch of May 31 last, I
                    have the honor to bring to the knowledge of your legation that the Haitian
                    Government approves willingly the decision taken by His Excellency Mr. Estrada
                    Palma to confide to the consular officers <pb facs="0759" n="679" xml:id="pg679"
                    /> of the United States in Haiti the mission to protect the citizens of the
                    Republic of Cuba residing in our territory, as well as their commercial
                    interests, until the appointment of Cuban consular agents.</p>
                <p>I profit by this occasion to renew to you, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jérémie</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Member of the Provisional Government Charged with
                            the Department of Foreign Relations.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
